  "answer": "The Nile Delta's August to October seasons of 2018 to 2026 average 882 hotspot-days, 53% below (50% to 55% below) the 1,864 of 2005 to 2017. It is not a steady low: 2023 came back to 1,706. Kafr El Sheikh is 61% below (60% to 64% below) and Sharqia 56% below (53% to 58% below): both fell by more than half. Kafr El Sheikh is 5 points further down, a gap smaller than what leaving out one season does to either figure, so whether it fell further: cannot tell. The lowest season is 2026 in Kafr El Sheikh and 2018 in Sharqia.",
